{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-202361-r4536308","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Gyudon (Japanese Beef and Rice Bowl)","sourcePageId":202361,"sourceRevision":"4536308","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-09-04T23:59:43Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Gyudon%20(Japanese%20Beef%20and%20Rice%20Bowl)&oldid=4536308","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:05:15.620Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Boiled recipes","Category:Japanese recipes","Category:Main course recipes","Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using beef","Category:Recipes using egg","Category:Recipes using fresh ginger","Category:Recipes using green onion","Category:Recipes using mirin","Category:Recipes using rice","Category:Recipes using sugar","Category:Recipes with images","Category:Recipes with metric units","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"25b686a5cc0723874d62e8bbfda09af5c057ed62f608dfb5d2a359d7f78256d0","sourceWikitext":"{{recipesummary\n| Category = Japanese recipes\n| Rating = 2\n| Difficulty = 3\n| Image = [[file:Gyudon by jetalone in Higashi-Ginza, Tokyo.jpg|300px]]\n}}\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of Japan|Japan]]\n\n'''Gyudon''', often literally translated as 'beef bowl', is a Japanese dish consisting of rice topped with beef and onion simmered in a mildly sweet sauce flavored with dashi, soy sauce, and mirin. It also often includes shirataki noodles. Gyudon is a very popular food in Japan, and it is commonly served with beni shōga (pickled ginger), shichimi seasoning, and a side dish of [[Cookbook:Miso Soup|miso soup]]. ''Gyū'' means \"cow\" or \"beef\", and ''don'' is short for ''donburi'', the Japanese word for \"bowl\".\n\n==Ingredients==\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Egg|eggs]]\n* 200 [[Cookbook:Gram|g]] thinly-[[Cookbook:Slicing|sliced]] [[Cookbook:Beef|beef]]\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]], cut into wedges\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoon]] [[Cookbook:Sake|sake]]\n* 1 tablespoon [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]]\n* 1 tablespoon [[Cookbook:Mirin|mirin]]\n* 2 tablespoons [[Cookbook:Soy Sauce|soy sauce]]\n* 100 [[Cookbook:Milliliter|ml]] [[Cookbook:Water|water]]\n* ½ teaspoon [[Cookbook:Dashi (Japanese Soup Stock)|dashi]]\n* 5 g [[Cookbook:Ginger|ginger]], grated\n* [[Cookbook:Steamed Rice|Steamed rice]]\n* Beni shōga (pickled [[Cookbook:Ginger|ginger]])\n* Shichimi seasoning\n* [[Cookbook:Green Onion|Scallions]], [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n\n==Procedure==\n# Cover the eggs in [[Cookbook:Boiling|boiling]] water, and let them sit for 20 minutes so they are soft inside and not hard. Carefully peel off the shell.\n# [[Cookbook:Boiling|Boil]] the beef and drain the water.\n# Combine sake, mirin, soy sauce, and sugar in a [[Cookbook:Frying Pan|frying pan]]. Stir over at medium heat.\n# Add beef and cook. Before all the sauce evaporates, remove the beef.\n# Add water, dashi, grated ginger, and onions to the sauce. Cover and boil.\n# Mix in the beef.\n# Put the steamed rice in a bowl, and top with the sauced meat.\n# Arrange the soft egg and pickled ginger on top. Top with scallions and shichimi seasoning.\n\n== External links ==\n[http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=F1mvYnRJX70 Video instructions]\n\n[[Category:Japanese recipes|Gyudon]]\n[[Category:Recipes using beef|Gyudon]]\n[[Category:Recipes using rice]]\n[[Category:Boiled recipes]]\n[[Category:Main course recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes with metric units]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using fresh ginger]]\n[[Category:Recipes using green onion]]\n[[Category:Recipes using mirin]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Gyudon (Japanese Beef and Rice Bowl)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"2 eggs","sourceText":"2 eggs","amountText":"2 eggs","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"200 g thinly-sliced beef","sourceText":"200 g thinly-sliced beef","amountText":"200 g thinly-sliced beef","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"½ onion, cut into wedges","sourceText":"½ onion, cut into wedges","amountText":"½ onion, cut into wedges","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"1 tablespoon sake","sourceText":"1 tablespoon sake","amountText":"1 tablespoon sake","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"1 tablespoon sugar","sourceText":"1 tablespoon sugar","amountText":"1 tablespoon sugar","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"1 tablespoon mirin","sourceText":"1 tablespoon mirin","amountText":"1 tablespoon mirin","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"2 tablespoons soy sauce","sourceText":"2 tablespoons soy sauce","amountText":"2 tablespoons soy sauce","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-8","name":"100 ml water","sourceText":"100 ml water","amountText":"100 ml water","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-9","name":"½ teaspoon dashi","sourceText":"½ teaspoon dashi","amountText":"½ teaspoon dashi","amount":null,"unit"